WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.790
- I don't know what it's taste
like when it's become Jesus--

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:03.623
- These are the kinds
of things that make--

00:00:03.623 --> 00:00:06.310
- There was a pig situation,
I was like this feels off.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.667
- So I'm eating this--

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.290
- There was one Ramadan
where basically it was

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:19.030
my lag year between college,
my internship, and grad school

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.070
and somehow it seems like
when you have nothing

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:23.210
to do during Ramadan, fasting is easier

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.050
but it's actually the quite opposite.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.460
Being sort of in a routine
and doing your daily life

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.080
it's a lot easier to fast and so I

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.290
was really struggling
fasting during this time.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.540
My sister also had a
lag year so one Ramadan

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.580
we just basically would sleep all day

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.070
which is like not the point and
then we would break our fast

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:44.070
and then until then we
watched Criminal Minds

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.260
until sahur time, then we'd eat

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:48.650
and then we'd do it all over again.

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.610
And that was my normal
life for an entire month.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.570
Like nine seasons and there
was one particular episode

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.610
that there was a pig
situation and we were like

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.150
this feels off, this is not
something we should be watching.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.650
It was a really scary episode.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:03.043
People were feeding women
to pigs in this episode.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.470
That's not my proudest
Ramadan, but it is what it is.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:10.010
- Okay, okay, one Ramadan I
was in the awkward position

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:12.660
of deciding whether to break my fast

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.233
with an unconsecrated communion host.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:18.000
I went to a Catholic high school.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.500
For all the non-Catholics out there,

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.700
during mass Catholics take communion,

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:25.040
it's a host, a wafer and some wine.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.970
The Priests like whisper a prayer

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:31.110
over the host, turn it
into Jesus, his body

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.140
and then they turn the
wine into his blood.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.810
So I wasn't sure how to
convert, but I really wanted

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:38.950
to know what that wafer tasted
like and everyone knew it.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.210
Everyone knew the Muslim wanted

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:41.410
to know what the wafer tasted like.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:44.440
So Ramadan of my junior
year, this nun decides

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.250
to make my dreams come true.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:49.270
She breaks into the
school communion stash,

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:52.160
she runs off with a wafer just for me.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:56.383
She's like here it is, the
wafer, the wafer of your dreams.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.483
And I'm thinking, oh my god, I'm fasting.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:00.470
What am I gonna do?

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.960
Everyone's watching me, I think
everyone knew I was fasting.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.533
I had like Ramadan breath,
anyway, I'm eating it.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:08.770
And I don't know what it's taste like

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:10.900
when it's become Jesus but before

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.303
it becomes Jesus, it
tastes like old paper.

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:15.440
So I'm thinking to myself, you know what,

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:18.920
damn I should've asked for
the wine too, you know.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.770
If you're gonna go down, might
as well go down in flames.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:27.350
- So a couple of years ago
my best friend and I decided

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:29.820
that for Iftar rather than just having

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.600
you know, like a regular dinner spread,

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.313
we would host a thing
called Pizza Olympics.

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:36.340
Where we would order pizza from any place

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:38.330
that we could think of,
have it all delivered

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.920
to one location and then we
would make all of our guests

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.270
have a slice of each
pizza and then rank them

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:44.650
to determine which one is the best

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.890
because we love science and we love pizza

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.430
and these are the kinds
of things that make

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.770
a lot of sense when you
haven't eaten for 14 hours.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:53.240
So we set up our party,
all the pizza comes.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.760
It's all Margherita because it

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.380
has to be standardized obviously.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.683
This is the Olympics, we care about rigor.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.970
We lay it out and people
are getting in line,

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.673
getting their pizza and eating it.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.870
And then there's just
this guy who's a friend

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.140
of someone else's looking at the pizza

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.233
with like kind of the judgy face.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.320
And because I'm trying to be gracious

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.420
because it is the spirit of Ramadan,

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.033
I ask him, hey please take a
plate please help yourself.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.640
And then he tells me that
he doesn't like pizza,

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.060
it's disgusting and it's kind of fattening

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.083
and do we have anything else
like salad that he would eat.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.253
Who eats salad, nobody
eat salad during Ramadan.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.690
The point is fried things
and that's when I learned

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:35.660
the real lesson of Ramadan
is that while not eating food

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.500
and not drinking water can be challenging,

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.453
not being really shady is very hard.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:43.334
(playful music)

